  "name": "with requireConsent, an install refused because consent was closed is sent once when consent is granted later in the same launch, never twice and not after forgetMe",
  "source": "Swift Engine.swift installDeferred (released in setConsent(true)); Android parity follow-up to run-2 U2. Without it an app that gets consent after launch sends no install until the next launch. The deferral is launch-scoped (in memory): INSTALL_SENT_KEY stops a second send, a denial releases nothing, and forgetMe ends it.",
